# act configuration for fluxion local CI validation
#
# Usage:
#   act -l                                    # list available jobs
#   act -j fmt-clippy                         # run one job
#   act                                       # run all triggered jobs for current event
#
# Why catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04 (medium image):
# - Ships pre-installed rustup + cargo + node + python + common build tools
# - Much faster than pulling plain ubuntu + apt-installing everything
# - The :full-latest image pulls from ghcr.io which can hit anonymous rate limits;
#   :act-22.04 is on Docker Hub which has more lenient limits.
#
# Pin the image so contributors don't hit "missing toolchain" CI-shape bugs.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04

# Use linux/amd64 — avoids ARM emulation on Apple Silicon running x86 Docker
--container-architecture linux/amd64

# Default working directory inside the container matches GH Actions
--defaultbranch develop

# Verbose by default; pass -q to silence
--verbose
